course: dictionary
lesson: 11607
title: Sharing out with apportion
level: primary-6
stars: 3
explain: Apportion is a formal word. It means to divide something and share it out among people. Look at the words around it to find its meaning: «The teacher will apportion the sweets equally among the class» tells you that the sweets are being shared out, and that each child gets the same amount.
explain: Apportion can also be used with blame. «The head teacher had to apportion blame after the broken window.» Here the clues are blame and broken window. To apportion blame means to decide how much each person is responsible for something bad.
explain: In maths, apportion often means share in a given ratio, not always equally. «Apportion 60 pounds between Ann and Ben in the ratio 2:1» means Ann gets two parts and Ben gets one part. Two parts of 60 is 40, and one part is 20. To check, add your answers: 40 + 20 must make 60.
fact: Apportion means to divide something and share it out among people.
fact: To apportion blame means to decide how much each person is responsible for something bad.
fact: The verb forms are apportion, apportions, apportioned and apportioning.
fact: «Apportion 60 pounds between Ann and Ben in the ratio 2:1» gives Ann 40 pounds and Ben 20 pounds.
fact: Apportion is a formal word, so you will often meet it in exams, maths problems and the news.
exercise: «Mum will apportion the cake equally among the four of us.» What does apportion mean here? | Eat all of it at once | Throw it away | *Divide and share out | Weigh it on the scales
exercise: «The head teacher had to apportion blame after the broken window.» What does apportion blame mean? | Forget who did it | Hide the blame from everyone | Say sorry for everything | *Decide how much each person is responsible for the bad thing
exercise: «Apportion 60 pounds between Ann and Ben in the ratio 2:1.» How much does Ann get? | 30 pounds | 60 pounds | 20 pounds | *40 pounds
test: «Ella had 12 sweets to apportion equally between her 3 friends.» How many sweets does each friend get? | *4 | 9 | 6 | 3
test: «The prize money will be apportioned between the three winners.» What does apportioned mean? | Given back to the judge | Lost | Counted twice | *Shared out
exam: Which word is closest in meaning to apportion? | shout | *divide | forget | multiply
